      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe here we have one more index validation check before assignment:\n```\n// SIM config change arrived before carrier service change, abandon uid for invalid slot\nif (mLogicalSlot \u003e\u003d mModemCount) return;\nmCarrierServiceUid[mLogicalSlot] \u003d carrierServiceUid;\n```\n\nmLogicalSlot was assigned with slot during registration. By the time the callback arrives, the mModemCount may have been updated.\n\nThe case I am worried of is from DSDS \u003d\u003e Single SIM switching, depend on the ordering of the two events below:\n- CarrierPrivilegesTracker detected the SIM state changed and may trigger the onCarrierServiceChanged callback\n- CarrierPrivilegeAuthenticator received the ACTION_MULTI_SIM_CONFIG_CHANGED broadcast receiver and updated mModemCount (and mCarrierServiceUid).\n\nIn theory, the former event should arrive first. But SIM state change in Telephony is a known caoise. It wouldn\u0027t hurt to perform the additional check to stand on the safe side.",
